S108 src=cite kid=K003 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Ordering of real numbers: for every real x, exactly one of x > 0, x = 0, x < 0 is true; sums and products of nonnegative numbers are nonnegative; x squared is >= 0 for every real x.
S109 src=cite kid=K004 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Euclid's postulates: (1) a straight line segment can be drawn joining any two points; (2) any line segment can be extended indefinitely; (3) a circle can be drawn with any center and any radius; (4) all right angles are congruent; (5) parallel postulate: given a line and a point not on it, exactly one line through the point is parallel to the given line.
