S112 src=cite kid=K101 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Divisibility: for integers a and b with a != 0, 'a divides b' (written a|b) holds if and only if (iff) there is an integer c with b = a * c.
S113 src=cite kid=K102 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Prime number: an integer p > 1 whose only positive divisors are 1 and p.
S114 src=cite kid=K103 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Composite number: an integer n > 1 that is not prime.
S115 src=cite kid=K104 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Congruence: for a positive integer n, 'a is congruent to b modulo n' (written a ≡ b (mod n)) holds if and only if (iff) n divides (a - b).
S116 src=cite kid=K105 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Rational number: a real number that can be written as p/q with integers p and q != 0.
S117 src=cite kid=K105 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Irrational number: a real number that is not rational.
S118 src=cite kid=K106 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Factorial: 0! = 1, and n! = n * (n-1)! for n >= 1.
S119 src=cite kid=K106 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Binomial coefficient: C(n,k) = n!/(k! * (n-k)!) for integers 0 <= k <= n.
S120 src=cite kid=K107 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Even and odd: an integer n is even if n = 2k for some integer k; n is odd if n = 2k + 1 for some integer k.
S121 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Triangle: three non-collinear points together with the segments joining them.
S122 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Interior angle: the angle inside the triangle at a vertex.
S123 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Median: the segment from a vertex to the midpoint of the opposite side.
S124 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Isosceles triangle: a triangle with (at least) two equal sides.
S125 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Right triangle: a triangle with one 90-degree angle.
S126 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Parallel lines: lines in a plane that never meet.
S127 src=cite kid=K109 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Perfect square: an integer of the form m^2 for some integer m.
S128 src=cite kid=K110 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Probability (finite, equally likely outcomes): the probability of an event is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the number of total outcomes.
S129 src=cite kid=K201 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Fundamental theorem of arithmetic: every integer greater than 1 is a product of prime numbers, uniquely up to order.
S130 src=cite kid=K202 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Euclid's lemma: if p is a prime number and p divides the product a * b, then p divides a or p divides b.
S131 src=cite kid=K203 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Bezout's identity: for integers a and b, there are integers x and y with a*x + b*y = gcd(a,b).
S132 src=cite kid=K204 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Pigeonhole principle: if more than n items are placed into n boxes, some box contains at least 2 items.
S133 src=cite kid=K205 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Pythagorean theorem: in a right triangle with legs a, b and hypotenuse c, a^2 + b^2 = c^2.
S134 src=cite kid=K206 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: There are infinitely many prime numbers.
S135 src=cite kid=K207 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Algebraic identities: (a+b)^2 = a^2+2ab+b^2; (a-b)^2 = a^2-2ab+b^2; a^2-b^2 = (a-b)(a+b), for all real numbers a and b.
S136 src=cite kid=K208 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Vertical angles are equal.
S137 src=cite kid=K208 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: If a transversal cuts two parallel lines, alternate interior angles are equal.
S138 src=cite kid=K209 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Triangle congruence criteria: SAS, ASA, SSS.
S139 src=cite kid=K209 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: (If two triangles satisfy any one of these criteria, all corresponding sides and angles are equal.)
S140 src=cite kid=K210 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Midpoint theorem: the segment joining the midpoints of two sides of a triangle is parallel to the third side and half its length.
